-- A copattern definition (alone, or with others of a mutual group grp, a list of signature
-- indices) is λs and lines over a record. Each field's term is guarded: a definition of the group
-- stands only as the head of a call (applied to arguments not mentioning the group, at any
-- dimensions), the whole term or under a λ, a line, a pair, a constructor, a case's or a system's
-- branch, or a let's body; never as an argument or eliminated. Then the definition is checked at
-- its type, its own calls at their declared types: a guarded call is productive, so the value
-- exists at every depth, and its boundary holds at every depth since it holds at each field.
in-grp grp n = lany (λ m → %weq n m) grp
